{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ObtuseWedgeDegenerate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ObtuseWedgeDegenerate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemeTiling"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.gamma_chord_of_mem_beta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.gamma_chord_of_mem_beta","kind":"theorem","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L454-L467","doc":"**The `γ`-chord for a point of `W_β` outside `W_sub`.**  Mirror: the upper\nedge is shared with `W_sub`, and the lower is\n`wedgeAt_beta_perp_lower_of_obtuse`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.gamma_chord_of_mem_alpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.gamma_chord_of_mem_alpha","kind":"theorem","line":439,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L439-L452","doc":"**The `γ`-chord for a point of `W_α` outside `W_sub`.**  Both cone\nconditions come from `W_α` itself: the lower edge is shared with `W_sub`, and\nthe upper is `wedgeAt_alpha_perp_upper_of_obtuse`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.gamma_chord_of_notMem_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.gamma_chord_of_notMem_sub","kind":"theorem","line":413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L413-L437","doc":"**The `γ`-chord from non-membership in `W_sub`.**  Given the two cone\nconditions, `w ∉ W_sub` forces the triangle's `γ`-chord inequality, non-strictly.\nThe `≤` is sharp: `w` on the chord line lies in neither side, which is why the\ndecomposition is an a.e. identity and not a set equality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_beta_perp_lower_of_obtuse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_beta_perp_lower_of_obtuse","kind":"theorem","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L362-L396","doc":"**`W_β` lies inside `W_sub`'s cone** — here it is the LOWER-edge half that\nneeds work, the mirror of the `W_α` case.\n\n`W_β = wedgeAt R (t+2γ+2α+β) β` has upper edge at `t+2γ+2α+2β = t+2π`, which is\nalready `W_sub`'s upper edge, so that half is free.  Its lower edge is at\n`t+2γ+2α`, an angle `2α` short of `W_sub`'s lower edge `t+2γ`.  The SAME\nthree-angle relation supplies the gap, rearranged:\n\n    sin(2β)·perp_{t+2γ} = sin(2α+2β)·perp_{t+2γ+2α} − sin(2α)·perp_{t+2π},\n\nnow (positive)·(positive) − (positive)·(negative) > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_alpha_perp_upper_of_obtuse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_alpha_perp_upper_of_obtuse","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L322-L360","doc":"**`W_α` lies inside `W_sub`'s cone** — the upper-edge half, which is the\npart `wedgeAt_upper` cannot reach.\n\nFor `w ∈ wedgeAt R (t+2γ+α) α` the wedge's own edges give\n`perp_{t+2γ} > 0` (lower) and `perp_{t+2γ+2α} < 0` (upper).  `W_sub`'s upper\nedge sits at `t + 2π`, a further `2β` on.  The three-angle relation at\n`φ = t+2γ+2α`, `p = 2α`, `q = 2β` reads\n\n    sin(2α)·perp_{t+2π} = sin(2α+2β)·perp_{t+2γ+2α} − sin(2β)·perp_{t+2γ},\n\nwhose right side is (positive)·(negative) − (positive)·(positive) < 0.  All\nthree sines are positive because `α`, `β` and `α+β` are acute — which is exactly\nwhat `γ` obtuse buys. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perp_three_angle_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perp_three_angle_relation","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L311-L320","doc":"**The three-angle `perp` relation.**  Three linear functionals on a\ntwo-dimensional space satisfy one relation; written at directions\n`φ − p`, `φ`, `φ + q` its coefficients are `sin q`, `−sin(p+q)`, `sin p`.\n`perp_sign_relation` is this identity at the triangle's own angles. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_sub_lt_chord_beta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_sub_lt_chord_beta","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L280-L296","doc":"**The `W_β` companion of `wedgeAt_sub_lt_chord_alpha`.**\n`t + 2γ + 2α + β = (t+γ+π) + α` because `γ = π − α − β`, so this is the mirror\nshift at `δ = α`, with bound `R cos((α+β) − α) = R cos β` — exactly `W_β`'s\nchord.  Together the two corollaries say `W_sub` lies under BOTH surviving\nwedges' chords. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_lt_chord_shift'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_lt_chord_shift'","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L247-L278","doc":"**The mirror shift**, in the `+δ` direction.  Same bound `R cos(ψ − δ)`,\nbut the positive quantity in the certificate is now `−⟨w,v_{θ+ψ}⟩`, supplied by\n`wedgeAt_upper`, where `wedgeAt_lt_chord_shift` used `wedgeAt_lower`:\n\n  cos ψ · (R cos(ψ−δ) − ⟨w,u_{θ+δ}⟩)\n      = cos(ψ−δ) · (R cos ψ − S)  +  (−⟨w,v_{θ+ψ}⟩) · sin δ\n\nDerived rather than assumed from symmetry — the two lemmas consume *different*\nedge bounds, so neither follows from the other by a rewrite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_sub_lt_chord_alpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_sub_lt_chord_alpha","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L224-L245","doc":"**The instance the obtuse decomposition needs**, and the reason\n`wedgeAt_lt_chord_shift` was written: the subtracted wedge `W_sub` sits under\n`W_α`'s chord.\n\n`W_sub = wedgeAt R (t+γ+π) (π−γ)` has half-angle `π−γ = α+β`, and\n`t + 2γ + α = (t+γ+π) − β` because `γ = π − α − β`.  So this is the shift\nlemma at `δ = β`, whose bound `R cos((α+β) − β) = R cos α` is exactly `W_α`'s\nchord.  Both hypotheses come free: `α+β < π/2` because `γ` is obtuse, and\n`0 ≤ β ≤ α+β` because `α > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_lt_chord_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_lt_chord_shift","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L200-L222","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.disjoint_wedgeAt_obtuse_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.disjoint_wedgeAt_obtuse_pair","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L162-L170","doc":"**In the obtuse configuration the two surviving wedges are disjoint.**\nNo new argument — the acute `disjoint_wedgeAt_adjacent` applies verbatim,\nbecause `γ` obtuse forces `α` and `β` acute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perp_coeff_signs_of_obtuse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.perp_coeff_signs_of_obtuse","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L136-L148","doc":"**The obtuse sign pattern of `perp_sign_relation`'s coefficients: `+ + −`.**\n\nThe relation itself is unchanged (it needs only `α + β + γ = π`); when `γ` is\nobtuse exactly one of its three coefficients is negative.  This is the precise\npoint at which the acute covering argument stops applying, and the precise\norigin of the minus sign in Milnor's subdivision. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.acute_of_obtuse_third","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.acute_of_obtuse_third","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L126-L134","doc":"**In an obtuse admissible triple the other two angles are acute.**\n`γ > π/2` and `α + β + γ = π` with `β > 0` force `α < π/2`, and symmetrically.\n(The corpus already records the `at_most_one_obtuse` half in\n`IdealTetObtuseReduction`; this is the quantitative form the sign argument\nneeds.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.sin_two_mul_neg_of_obtuse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.sin_two_mul_neg_of_obtuse","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L115-L124","doc":"**`sin 2γ < 0` for an obtuse `γ`.**  `sin (2γ) = 2 sin γ cos γ` with\n`sin γ > 0` and `cos γ < 0` on `(π/2, π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.origin_notMem_wedgeAt_of_obtuse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.origin_notMem_wedgeAt_of_obtuse","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L91-L98","doc":"**The apex itself is not in the obtuse wedge.**  A sanity corollary: the\ncircumcentre lies in `wedgeAt R θ ψ` for no obtuse `ψ`, whereas for acute `ψ`\nthe wedge is the isoceles triangle *with apex there*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_subset_far_halfplane_of_obtuse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_subset_far_halfplane_of_obtuse","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L83-L89","doc":"**The obtuse wedge is disjoint from the closed near half-plane** — the\ncontainment form of the lemma above.  In particular it contains no point of the\nray from the circumcentre in the direction `θ` its name refers to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_inner_neg_of_obtuse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.wedgeAt_inner_neg_of_obtuse","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L63-L81","doc":"**At an obtuse half-angle the wedge lies strictly on the FAR side of the\napex.**  The defining inequality `|⟨w,v⟩| < ⟨w,u⟩ · tan ψ` has a non-negative\nleft side, so it forces `⟨w,u⟩ · tan ψ > 0`; with `tan ψ < 0` that gives\n`⟨w,u⟩ < 0`.\n\nThis is the precise sense in which `wedgeAt` is acute-only: at `ψ > π/2` it does\nnot degenerate to something smaller, it moves to the other side of the\ncircumcentre. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.tan_neg_of_pi_div_two_lt_of_lt_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.tan_neg_of_pi_div_two_lt_of_lt_pi","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ObtuseWedgeDegenerate.lean#L53-L61","doc":"**`tan` is negative on `(π/2, π)`** — `sin > 0` and `cos < 0` there.\nMathlib names the `(-π/2, 0)` case (`Real.tan_neg_of_neg_of_pi_div_two_lt`) but\nnot this one. ","signatureChunk":0}]}